                <pb facs="0813" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg705"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Terrell reports the disapproval by the Sultan of the verbal agreement made
                    with the Sublime Porte that a refusal on the part of a naturalized citizen of
                    the United States born in Turkey to leave would be the only ground on which such
                    citizen could be imprisoned.</p>
            </div>
